amendmentsChecked.detail:
engine.ts:1233 enqueueMany:
- one synchronous requireStore gate;
- every shape and writable flag checked before any write;
- one inHand and one store.transaction, inserting in call order;
- one refreshCounts, one emit (tables plus OUTBOX_CHANNEL), one flush.

enqueue delegates to enqueueMany([input]), and useOutbox exposes enqueueMany. sales queue.ts builds the header plus its positive lines and calls enqueueMany once. It is the only enqueue call site in sales-app (grep).

leaveNow in all three apps sweeps on every sign-out. Sales computes kept = keptBy(end result) ?? keepQueue and calls forgetDrafts only when !kept.

Probe P2: a statement failing mid-transaction (the line's local insert) leaves _outbox, sales_orders and sales_order_lines empty, with pending 0 and no emit.

client.ts:326 signOutOnDevice runs in this order:
1. keeps the refresh token in memory;
2. bumps generation;
3. session.clearOnDevice() clears the cache synchronously and returns the platform-store removal promise;
4. calls leave(stored) in the same turn;
5. sends logout with the kept token only after leave settles, never awaited and never writing the session.

signIn awaits leaving.

refreshNow and switchDistributor discard and revoke a pair that arrives for an ended generation. The backend check: logout of a late pair hits an already revoked or rotated row, and switchTenant creates a new session row, so the next session is never revoked.

The three apps' api.ts add clearSession (storage.removeItem for the refresh and snapshot keys).

In all three apps leaveNow runs end({keepQueue, after: stored}), then sweep, then (sales) forgetDrafts, all inside signOutOnDevice. end() awaits after before any store call.

Send now still sends with the live session first. The forced-401 path is unchanged.
